  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1230 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nA strong high pressure ridge will remain steadfast across the \nregion, keeping hot and dry conditions across West Central Texas \nthrough the end of the weekend. By Sunday afternoon and Monday, a\nseries of embedded disturbances aloft will track through the area,\nbringing some increased shower and thunderstorm chances to the\narea through at least mid next week. The weakening of the upper-\nlevel ridge will allow for low to medium chances (20-50%) for\nprecipitation. A weak cold frontal boundary may be just strong \nenough to drop temperatures a few degrees for much of next week,\nwith highs in the upper 80s to mid 90s, and overnight lows in the\nmid 60s to low 70s.",
